A lot of it has to do with how easy each one is to obtain.

Grayswandir isn't trivial to obtain but is pretty much the best weapon in
vanilla, hands down.

Magicbane's instant limitless Elbereth, curse resistance, and MR make it
worthwhile for anyone who can get it.

Excalibur can be had by any lawful for a trivial cost since barrow wights
carry longswords.  It is "good enough" to ascend.

Snickersnee is the Samurai's guaranteed first gift; its damage is nearly
identical to Excalibur, and if a Sam somehow hasn't found a longsword by
the time he gets to an altar, it's trivial for him to get this instead
and be done with looking for weapons.

The Sceptre of Might isn't easy to get, but provides hungerless conflict
(broken in vanilla) and MR... and it isn't even all _that_ bad a weapon,
though you probably just want to lug it around instead.

Stormy's nice but just doesn't provide that much.  Mojo, Fire, and
Frosty all bust things up and require either an elaborate sacfest or a
wish... and none of them are worth wishing for.  (Contrast with
Magicbane and the Sceptre, whose additional non-weapon effects make them
well worth an early wish.)  

If you have to sit there saccin', well, that drags down time and potentially 
burns resources.  There's a lot to be said for the efficacy of "get in, 
get out, get done" -- if only because it removes the need for the player 
to spend a great deal of time and mental energy tracking side crap.

